  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b7fd-cc9e-4964-0a96" name="Hyksos (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #117 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The Hyksos tribes originated in Syria and Canaan and invaded Egypt in waves, conquering the old northern kingdom but not the southern, centred on Thebes. The warlords set themselves up as Pharaohs but were unable to stand against the resurgent Egyptians, who under Pharaoh Ahmose ejected them. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Hyksos]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Chariotry: up to 50% Infantry: At least 25% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
